<title>USA: Asarco Coeur d'Alene silver cost under $4/oz..</title>
<headline>Asarco Coeur d'Alene silver cost under $4/oz..</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Asarco Inc has reduced its costs in Idaho's  Couer d'Alene silver mining district to &quot;below the $4 (per ounce)  range,&quot; chief executive Richard Osborne said Friday.</p>
<p>When the company resumed production at the Coeur mine in Wallace,  Idaho, in May 1996, the company's costs were $5.75 an ounce, he told  reporters after Asarco's quarterly analysts' meeting, adding &quot;our  costs have dropped faster than the price of silver&quot; as mining operations  became more efficient.</p>
</text>
